course: dictionary
lesson: 4933
title: Impertinent: rude and cheeky
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Impertinent means rude, cheeky, and not showing proper respect, especially to an older person or someone in charge. Look at the clues in the sentence: «The King says the Cat may kiss his hand; the Cat answers "I'd rather not"; the King says "Don't be impertinent"». The King is in charge, and the Cat has answered back, so the King is saying the Cat is being cheeky.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. «Don't be rude» fits the King's words, so impertinent must mean rude. Alice uses the word too: «"You shouldn't make personal remarks," Alice said; "it's very rude."» Her words show the same meaning.
explain: The word also has an old, formal meaning: a remark that is impertinent is not relevant to what is being talked about. You can spot this from the topic. If someone says something that has nothing to do with the lesson, it is impertinent in that old sense. Most of the time, though, it means cheeky.
fact: Impertinent means rude and not showing proper respect.
fact: «An impertinent question» is a question that is rude or cheeky.
fact: «Don't be impertinent» means «Don't be cheeky».
fact: In old school stories, teachers punish impertinent pupils. Today we would say «cheeky» or «rude».
fact: In its old, formal sense, impertinent means not relevant to what is being talked about.
exercise: What does impertinent mean? | *Rude and not showing proper respect | Sleepy after a long day | Very tall | Polite and kind
exercise: What does «an impertinent question» mean? | A kind, gentle question | *A rude, cheeky question | A question about the weather
exercise: A pupil talks about football in a maths lesson. The teacher says the remark is impertinent. What does impertinent mean here? | Very kind | *Not relevant to what is being talked about | Very hungry | Very quiet
test: Alice says the Hatter's remarks are impertinent. Which word is closest in meaning? | *Rude | Happy | Quiet | Gentle
test: Which sentence uses impertinent correctly? | The sky was impertinent and bright blue | *The pupil was impertinent and answered the teacher back | The cake was impertinent and warm | The dog was impertinent and sleepy
exam: Which word means the same as impertinent? | Sleepy | Bright | *Cheeky | Gentle
